# La foresta, capitolo 1 (forest/forest_zone.gd). Un cue per cosa con cui si parla (il
# nome del tile), più arrive (l'atterraggio) ed exit (l'uscita della zona).

~ arrive
Grass. Cold, wet grass, under her cheek.
Above her, leaves. So many leaves the sky is only a few holes of light.
Trees everywhere. Taller than the house. Taller than anything.
Lethe: ...Where...?
Something sharp is still in her hand. A piece of the mirror.
It doesn't hurt yet.
=> END

# Selene scende dalla luna (forest_zone.gd, meet_selene): la prima scelta del capitolo.
# La verità accende la magia (learn_truth); la bugia no, ma la spada la sente.
~ selene_meet
A light comes down through the leaves. Small, curved. Like a piece of the moon.
It stops in front of her face. It hums.
Selene: Oh. You're awake. Good.
Selene: I'm Selene. I came down from your window. The moon in it.
Lethe: ...My window?
Selene: I've been watching your room for a long time. Every night, the same night.
Selene: Are you hurt?
- I'm fine.
	Lethe: I'm fine. [#wrong]
	set lies += 1
	Selene: ...Okay. If you say so.
	The glass in her hand catches the light. Like it heard her.
- My hand. The glass cut me.
	Lethe: My hand. The glass... it cut me.
	set truth += 1
	do learn_truth()
	Something warm opens in her palm. Not glass. Light.
	Selene: See? When you say it, it shines.
Selene: Come on. There's a path. I'll stay close.
=> END

~ mirror
if seen("mirror") == 0
	A small mirror, standing alone in the grass. A violet frame, like her dress.
	It reflects the moon. Not her.
	Lethe: Same glass as the one in my room...
	if selene_met()
		Selene: You can rest here. The glass remembers you.
		Selene: If you fall... you'll wake up in front of it. I promise.
else
	The moon in the mirror hasn't moved.
She rests a moment, close to the glass. Her heart loosens.
do rest()
=> END

# Quando il cuore è stretto del tutto (forest_zone.gd, die): si riparte dallo specchio.
~ wake_again
Lethe: ...
The mirror is cold against her back. She's still here.
if selene_met()
	Selene: You're back. ...You're back.
	Selene: Don't do that again. Please.
	- I'm okay.
		Lethe: I'm okay. [#wrong]
		set lies += 1
	- That hurt.
		Lethe: That hurt. A lot.
		set truth += 1
		Selene: I know. I felt it too.
=> END

~ brambles
Thorns, grown thick across the path. [shiver]Something glints behind them.[/shiver]
if knows_open()
	Lethe: ...Open.
	She pushes the branches aside, slowly, the way you open curtains in the morning.
	do open_brambles()
	if selene_met()
		Selene: You remembered how.
else
	Lethe: I can't get through. ...Not like this.
	if selene_met() and seen("brambles") == 0
		Selene: They grew shut. Like curtains nobody opens.
		Selene: Maybe someday you'll know how to open them.
=> END

~ old_stone
An old stone with a mark carved in it. It glows, a little.
if stone_teaches()
	Not an eye. A hand, open, pushing something aside.
	Lethe: ...Curtains.
	Lethe: I used to open them every morning. Then later. Then not at all.
	She puts her hand on the mark. It's warm.
	do learn_open()
	if selene_met()
		Selene: The roots that keep things shut... now they'll listen to you.
else
	Lethe: An eye. Or a moon.
	if selene_met()
		Selene: ...Someone was here before you.
		Selene: They didn't go back.
=> END

# Il primo nemico (forest_story.gd, first_enemy): tutto si ferma, la camera lo guarda.
~ first_enemy
Something moves in the dark between the trees. It has no face.
Lethe: ...That's the dark from under my bed.
Selene: Careful. It's not a moth. Not really. It's made of the things you didn't say.
if knows("truth_spark")
	Selene: You have the light, and the glass. Light is slower. Glass cuts both ways.
else
	Selene: You have the glass. Use it if you have to.
	Selene: It will want you to.
=> END

# Il ruscello del Lete. Con Selene: la sua prima bugia ("just a sip"), e una seconda
# occasione per la prima verità (se a Selene Lethe ha mentito, la magia arriva qui).
~ lethe
Black water, very still. It doesn't reflect anything.
It smells like sleep.
if not selene_met()
	Lethe: ...I'm not thirsty. [#wrong]
elif seen("lethe") == 0
	Selene: That's the Lethe. It runs through everything here.
	Selene: Just a sip. It stops hurting. [#wrong]
	- I'm not thirsty.
		Lethe: ...I'm not thirsty. [#wrong]
		set lies += 1
		Selene: ...Right. Neither am I.
	- It scares me.
		Lethe: It scares me. It's too quiet.
		set truth += 1
		do learn_truth()
		Selene: ...Yeah. Me too, a little.
else
	The water doesn't move. Selene stays close to her shoulder.
=> END

~ exit
The path goes on, deeper into the trees.
Somewhere ahead, something is white. Like bone. Like a dead tree.
if selene_met()
	Selene: ...There. Can you feel it? Something up ahead is very tired.
	Lethe: It looks like the plant on my windowsill.
	Selene: Then it's waiting for you.
=> END

# --- La radura dell'albero secco (zona "tree", forest_story.gd) ---------------------------

# La prima volta: la camera va sull'albero, con la luna sopra.
~ tree_arrive
In the middle of the clearing there is a tree. White, all of it. Like bone.
No leaves. The moon sits on its branches like it's waiting for something.
Lethe: ...That's my plant.
Lethe: The one on my windowsill. It got so big.
if selene_met()
	Selene: And so dry.
=> END

~ dead_tree
if seen("dead_tree") == 0
	The bark is cold and smooth. It sounds hollow when she touches it.
	One leaf. Only one, up high. Still green.
	if selene_met()
		Selene: When did you last water it?
		- I don't remember.
			Lethe: I don't remember. ...A long time ago.
			set truth += 1
			Selene: It's still holding on. Look. One leaf.
		- It was already dead.
			Lethe: It was already dead when I got it. [#wrong]
			set lies += 1
			Selene: ...Then why does it have a leaf?
	Under the roots, something breathes. Slow. Like someone asleep.
else
	The leaf is still there. Up high. Still green.
=> END

~ root_hole
A hole between the roots, going down into the dark. The air coming up is warm, and smells like earth.
if selene_met()
	Selene: Whatever is making it sad... it's down there.
- Go down.
	Lethe: ...Okay. Stay close.
	do go_down()
- Not yet.
	Lethe: Not yet.
=> END

# --- Il dungeon delle radici (forest_story.gd: enter_roots, saw_heart) -----------------------

~ roots_arrive
Down. Much further than the hole looked.
The air is warm and wet. The roots overhead move, a little. Like something breathing.
Lethe: ...It smells like the pot. The plant pot, when I still watered it.
if selene_met()
	Selene: I'll stay close. I can make a little light.
	Selene: Not much. But a little.
=> END

~ silver_frame
if seen("silver_frame") == 0
	A silver frame, hanging from a root. The glass is clean. Someone keeps it clean.
	There's no photo inside. Only a heart, drawn in pencil on the back of the paper.
	Lethe: Someone wiped the dust off. All the way down here.
	if selene_met()
		Selene: You can rest here. Like at the mirror.
else
	The pencil heart. The clean glass.
She rests, her back against the cool roots. Her heart loosens.
do rest()
=> END

~ root_heart
if seen("root_heart") == 0
	All the roots meet here, twisted into a knot as big as a bed.
	It beats. Slowly. Behind a crack in the bark, something glows violet.
	Lethe: It's alive. It looks dead, and it's alive.
	if selene_met()
		Selene: Everything dry is still waiting for water.
		Selene: Or for someone to say it out loud.
	do saw_heart()
else
	Slow. Steady. Still beating.
=> END

~ arena_gate
Roots, grown into a wall across the passage. Thick as arms.
Behind them, something big breathes in its sleep.
Lethe: Not yet. I can't open this. ...Not like this.
if selene_met()
	Selene: They lean away from the dark. Toward light.
	Selene: The lanterns, in the lantern room. Maybe if they were lit...
=> END

# Le lanterne di radice (passo 4): si accendono con la luce di Lethe; senza, le accende Selene.
~ root_lantern
Roots, woven shut around nothing. A lantern, cold.
if has_light()
	Lethe: It's waiting for light.
	if selene_met() and seen("root_lantern") == 0
		Selene: Yours. Throw it.
elif selene_met()
	Lethe: I don't have any light left.
	Selene: ...I do. A little.
	do selene_light_lantern()
	The lantern takes the light. Selene looks smaller, for a moment.
	Selene: There. I'm fine. [#wrong]
else
	Lethe: It's waiting for light. I don't have any.
=> END

# La tenda di radici: si apre col gesto Aprire, e la luna accende la lanterna dietro.
~ root_curtain
Thin roots hang from the ceiling, thick and still, like a curtain someone forgot to open.
Behind them, a cold draft. And something shaped like a lantern.
if knows_open()
	Lethe: ...Open.
	She pushes the roots aside. Moonlight falls through, from somewhere very far above.
	do open_curtain()
else
	Lethe: I can't- ...Not like this.
	if selene_met()
		Selene: The old stone, in the stone room. It was waiting for someone.
=> END

# Le tre lanterne accese: il cancello dell'arena si apre, lontano. Con la luce di Lethe, la veglia.
~ lanterns_lit
Three lanterns. The roots lean toward the light, all together.
Far away, something made of wood breathes out, and gives.
if has_light()
	The lanterns lean toward Lethe too. Their flames bend, and four small ones come loose.
	Lethe: ...They're warm.
	do learn_vigil()
	if selene_met()
		Selene: Four little flames. They'll keep watch with you.
elif selene_met()
	Selene: ...See? We didn't need it.
	Selene: The way to the deer is open.
=> END

~ watering_can
if seen("watering_can") == 0
	A small watering can, half buried in the earth. Blue. Never used.
	The price sticker is still on it.
	Lethe: ...I bought this. The week before.
	Lethe: I was going to start taking care of things. The plant first. Then me.
	if selene_met()
		Selene: What happened?
		- Nothing happened.
			Lethe: Nothing happened. That's the thing. Nothing happened, every day.
			set truth += 1
			Selene: ...That's the hardest kind.
		- I forgot.
			Lethe: I just forgot. [#wrong]
			set lies += 1
			Selene: ...
else
	The price sticker. She never peeled it off.
=> END

# --- I meccanismi del dungeon (forest/zone_puzzles.gd) ---------------------------------------

# La piastra nelle lanterne: Lethe ci sale sopra.
~ plate_handprint
A flat stone in the floor, with a handprint pressed into it. Small. A child's hand.
It sinks under her feet with a click. Somewhere close, roots pull back.
Lethe: ...My hands were that small, once.
if selene_met()
	Selene: The roots moved for you. They remember you.
=> END

~ thorns_gate
Roots, woven tight across the passage. They shiver when she comes close.
Behind them, in the dirt, something small glints.
Lethe: They're not dead. They're waiting.
if is_pressed("handprint") == false
	if selene_met()
		Selene: That flat stone in the floor, by the pebbles... it has a hand on it.
		Selene: Maybe it wants to be stepped on.
	else
		Lethe: There's a stone in the floor here, with a hand on it. ...Like a button.
=> END

# La chiave per terra, nel passaggio delle spine: ci si parla e si raccoglie.
~ old_key
Something glints in the dirt, half buried under the roots. A key. Old, and warm from the earth.
do take_key("old_key")
Lethe knows it before she even picks it up.
Lethe: ...This is mine. The key to my room.
Lethe: I keep it on the inside. So nobody can- So I can stay in.
if selene_met()
	Selene: Then you know which door it opens.
=> END

# La chiave, presa senza dialogo (per sicurezza: di solito si raccoglie parlandoci).
~ old_key_found
An old key, warm from the earth. Lethe knows it before she even looks.
Lethe: ...This is mine. The key to my room.
Lethe: I keep it on the inside. So nobody can- So I can stay in.
if selene_met()
	Selene: Then you know which door it opens.
=> END

~ bedroom_door
if door_open("bedroom")
	The door stands open. Her own door, down here, and the dark behind it.
elif has_key("old_key")
	A door. Painted wood, a brass handle, roots grown all over it.
	It's her door. Her bedroom door. The scratch near the handle is still there.
	Lethe: ...It's locked. From the inside.
	- Use the key.
		Lethe: I locked it. Every night. Then every day.
		Lethe: ...I never thought I'd be the one outside.
		do open_door("bedroom")
	- Not yet.
		Lethe: Not yet.
else
	A door. Painted wood, a brass handle, roots grown all over it.
	It's her door. Her bedroom door, here under the tree.
	Lethe: Locked. ...Of course it's locked.
	if selene_met()
		Selene: There's a key somewhere. There always is.
=> END

~ shoebox
if box_open("shoebox")
	The shoebox is empty now. Only the drawings are left, and the other bracelet.
else
	A shoebox, half buried under the roots. The one that lived under her bed.
	Lethe: I put things in here. Things I didn't want to look at anymore.
	- Open it.
		Drawings. A ticket for a concert she never went to.
		Two friendship bracelets, the red thread coming loose. One was never given.
		Lethe: We made them together. Two each. I never gave her hers.
		Lethe: She stopped writing after a while. ...I stopped answering first.
		if selene_met()
			Selene: You can keep the thread. It's still strong.
		do open_box("shoebox")
	- Leave it buried.
		Lethe: ...Leave it.
=> END
